<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Viterbo (1267)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1267">1267</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Viterbo was concluded in May 1267 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>, the deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> emperor Baldwin II and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-villehardouin">William II of Villehardouin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, under the auspices of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-iv">Pope Clement IV</a>. William accepted Charles as suzerain, and his daughter Isabella married Charles's son Philip, so that Achaea passed to the Angevin kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> in 1278.</p></div>
